				33
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Maintain): Refactor build system into configuration-driven CLI with Rhai scripting\n\nReplace the legacy environment-variable-based build orchestration with a robust, configuration-driven CLI system. This overhaul introduces a unified `maintain` binary capable of handling both build and run workflows via subcommands, profile aliases, and dynamic Rhai scripting.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- **Architecture**: Added `TargetArchitecture` struct with support for macOS (Intel/Apple Silicon), Linux, and Windows triples.\n- **Build System**: Replaced static logic with `Build/CLI.rs` featuring subcommands (`build`, `list-profiles`, `resolve`, `validate`) and layered environment resolution (templates -> shell -> profile -> CLI overrides).\n- **Run System**: Introduced `Run/` module mirroring build architecture for development workflows with hot-reload and watch capabilities.\n- **Scripting**: Integrated Rhai engine (`Build/Rhai/`) to execute profile-specific scripts for dynamic environment generation, allowing complex logic without recompilation.\n- **Tooling**: Enhanced `JsonEdit` and `TomlEdit` utilities for safe, atomic updates to `tauri.conf.json` and `Cargo.toml` during build prep.\n- **Documentation**: Added extensive examples and integration tests verifying Rhai script outputs against expected environment variables.\n\nThis enables flexible, per-profile build configurations defined in `.vscode/land-config.json`, reducing shell script reliance and improving cross-platform consistency.",
			"SHA": "968a8a6e76d8221a7e5f946f8522288adc6b7900"
		},
